@api = http://localhost:3001

### Initial login. Use your own credentials; do not save them in this file.
POST {{api}}/scrape
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{espnUsername}}",
  "password": "{{espnPassword}}",
  "league": "IFHL",
  "sport": "hockey"
}

### If ESPN requests verification, reuse the challengeId from the 409 response.
POST {{api}}/scrape/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
  "code": "{{verificationCode}}"
}

### Automated runs reuse the sessionToken returned after the verified login.
# Keep this token in your scheduler's secret configuration, not in source control.
# No email/password/code is needed while ESPN accepts the saved browser session.
# A 401 ESPN_REAUTH_REQUIRED means a fresh verified login is necessary.
# Run only one scrape at a time per session. Use the same server/persistent session directory.
POST {{api}}/scrape
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionToken": "{{sessionToken}}",
  "league": "IFHL",
  "sport": "hockey"
}
